# Implementation Plan - Phase 55: Export and Import Setlists

## Overview
Phase 55 adds setlist Export and Import capabilities to KeryxPro, allowing users to back up setlists or transfer them to another machine running KeryxPro. The existing "Manage Setlists" top menu item will be converted into a dropdown menu containing **Import**, **Export**, and **Delete History**.

---

## User Requirements & Flow Summary
1. **Manage Setlist Dropdown Menu**:
   - In `CustomTitleBar`, convert the `'Manage Setlists'` menu item into a dropdown (`SubmenuButton`).
   - Dropdown Menu Options:
     - **Import**: Opens a popup dialog to browse and import a setlist JSON file.
     - **Export**: Opens a popup showing available setlists (sorted newest first, with date filter, latest setlist selected by default). Selecting setlists and clicking Export opens a folder picker to save individual `.json` files.
     - **Delete History**: Opens the existing setlist management popup to delete old setlists.

2. **Strict Constraints**:
   - No extra UI elements or buttons beyond specified requirements.
   - Maintain existing styling (`0xFF1E1E2E` dark theme, purple accent, standard dialog borders).
   - No changes to existing functionality outside the specified scope.

---

## User Approvals & Assumptions (Explicit Presumptions)

Please review and confirm the following assumptions:

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Menu Transformation**: The current single top menu item `Manage Setlists` in `custom_title_bar.dart` will become a `SubmenuButton` with 3 items: `Import`, `Export`, and `Delete History`.
> 2. **Delete History Popup**: Clicking `Delete History` opens `ManageSetlistsDialog`, which is the existing setlist deletion dialog with date filtering.
> 3. **Default Export Selection**: In the Export popup, setlists are sorted by `lastModified` descending (newest first), and the topmost (latest) setlist is checked/selected by default upon opening.
> 4. **Portable Setlist Export JSON**: To ensure setlists can be imported into KeryxPro on **another machine**, the exported JSON file will include:
>    - Setlist name, syncId, lastModified timestamp
>    - Item sequence order (`itemOrder`), image entries (`imageEntries`), favorites status (`favorites`)
>    - Full song data payload (syncId, title, author, lyrics, backgroundUrl) for songs included in the setlist.
>    - When imported on another machine, any missing songs will be automatically upserted into the target machine's Isar song database so the setlist renders cleanly without missing song references.
> 5. **Import Overwrite/Upsert**: Importing a setlist with an existing setlist name in Isar will update/upsert that setlist.

